# Pin every text file to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Everything committed here is already LF. This keeps it that way
# regardless of a contributor's core.autocrlf setting, which on Windows
# otherwise checks files out as CRLF — and a CRLF working copy makes
# `gofmt -l` report the whole file as unformatted, so `make lint` fails
# on files nobody touched.
#
# eol=lf rather than plain `text` so the working tree matches the
# repository on every platform: shell scripts under scripts/ are run
# through Git Bash on Windows and bash on CI, and CRLF breaks the
# shebang on Linux with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M".

* text=auto eol=lf

*.go     text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

*.exe binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
